From 141e8914262f7d51880937de4ddd7722e29ed5d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:47:12 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(doctor): close the review's argv leaks and over-masks;
 drop the filesystem check

Adversarial review of the fail-closed mask found leaks by position and
name, over-masking of real identifiers and a host-dependent path check.

Leaks closed:
- shell text: leading NAME=value env words and the first word are judged
  by name; a NAME=command value (ssh -o ProxyCommand=sshpass -p ...) is
  read as an assignment before it is split as a command
- grouped keys (ABCD-EF12-..., ab12_cd34_..., three+ equal groups),
  case/digit flip density, and long all-caps clusters judged as generated
- paths and URLs judged component by component with the full identifier
  rules (known ids inside, chunk checks), base64 pieces cut by "/" or "#"
  judged together, shell-unsafe symbols in a component masked
- symbol passwords: !^$* or several of &#%@ in a name (globs and npm
  @scope/pkg@version exempt)
- secret words passphrase/authorization/jwt/hmac and whole parts
  pass/pw/otp/creds; Go-style -password and Java -Dapi.key= flags;
  curl -b cookies; user:pass@host with an undotted host; the argument
  after a secret flag is its value unless it is a kebab-case --flag;
  mechanism words (oauth, header) only after auth-only flags; a path after
  a secret flag only when it looks like a file of 2+ directories
- long flags need a name that reads as one (urlsafe tokens start with -)

Over-masks fixed: workflow, launchctl, example.com, amazonaws hosts,
iOS/gRPC/eBPF, ExperimentalJSProfiler, Hermes ids inside paths, count flags
(--cap-tokens, --tokens-per-delta), --token-endpoint, non-ASCII words.

The "path exists here" shortcut is gone: it showed /tmp=SECRET and
~/SECRET, made output differ by host and user, and could block on a stale
mount. Letter-pair table rebuilt from the dictionary plus repo, process and
host vocabulary. Docstring states the measured rates and limits.

Tests: rewritten as one file with imports on top and a seeded RNG per test;
fuzz over 15 shapes x 4 positions x 4 lengths with the measured ceilings;
the two rows the previous commit edited are restored as explicit
"masked by design" checks (full commits, digests, hex session folders);
home-directory rows restored now that nothing touches the filesystem.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
